4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.675
Today we learn about HIV Prevention and Stigma. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.128 --> 00:00:22.094
HIV. Say it with me. HIV!

6
00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:29.273
Prevention. Say it with me. Prevention!

7
00:00:32.773 --> 00:00:36.140
Testing. Say it with me. Testing!

8
00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:43.446
Treatment. Say it with me. Treatment!

9
00:00:46.947 --> 00:00:50.913
Viral load. Say it with me. Viral load!

10
00:00:54.404 --> 00:00:58.121
Condoms. Say it with me. Condoms!

11
00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:05.400
Stigma. Say it with me. Stigma!

12
00:01:08.906 --> 00:01:13.323
Human rights. Say it with me. Human rights!

13
00:01:16.855 --> 00:01:31.367
HIV prevention includes condoms, testing, and never sharing needles. With treatment, a person's viral load can become undetectable, and they cannot pass HIV on through sex. Stigma harms people and human rights.

14
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:34.750
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:40.925
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.975 --> 00:01:42.125
Testing!

17
00:01:43.072 --> 00:01:48.339
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.389 --> 00:01:49.539
Stigma!

19
00:01:50.477 --> 00:02:00.095
Did you know? 'Undetectable = Untransmittable' (U=U) means people with an undetectable viral load do not pass HIV on through sex!

20
00:02:00.145 --> 00:02:02.622
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:12.117
Think and answer. How does treatment change life for people living with HIV?

22
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.317
Great answer!

23
00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:19.103
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
